<%- include("partials/head") %>
<%- include("partials/header") %>
<%- include("partials/nav") %>

<main class="resume-layout">
  <%- include("partials/contactModal") %>

  <article class="project-detail">
    <header class="card project-detail-hero">
      <a href="/projects" class="project-back-link">Back to projects</a>
      <p class="project-tag">Local AI / 3D Printing · Work in Progress</p>
      <h1>PrintTune</h1>
      <p>
        A local-first advisory platform for FDM 3D printers. PrintTune combines
        structured printer, slicer, filament and calibration data with
        deterministic diagnostics, local knowledge search and a German-first
        conversational AI assistant.
      </p>

      <div class="project-detail-actions">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/STU6266/PrintTune"
          class="project-link project-link-primary"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          GitHub
        </a>
        <span class="project-status">Alpha</span>
        <span class="project-status">Local-first</span>
        <span class="project-status">No live demo</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="project-detail-grid">
      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          PrintTune is being built as a desktop advisory system for FDM 3D
          printers. Its purpose is to collect printer and hardware configuration,
          slicer information, filament data, calibration results, diagnostic
          rules and local knowledge so users can get safer, more structured help
          while tuning and troubleshooting their printer.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Tech Stack</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Desktop/UI: Electron, React, TypeScript, Vite</li>
          <li>Storage/Data: node:sqlite, SQLite, FTS5</li>
          <li>Validation: JSON Schema, Ajv, Zod</li>
          <li>AI: Ollama behind an AIProvider abstraction</li>
          <li>Testing/Tooling: pnpm workspaces, Vitest, React Testing Library, Playwright</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Architecture Flow</h2>
        <p>
          The Alpha is read-only with respect to printer firmware/settings and
          imported source files. It should explain evidence and guide manual
          steps, not automatically control the printer.
        </p>
        <ol class="engineering-flow" aria-label="PrintTune engineering flow">
          <li>Printer / slicer / filament / calibration data</li>
          <li>Validation and domain models</li>
          <li>Local SQLite storage</li>
          <li>Rules, knowledge packages and FTS5 search</li>
          <li>AIProvider / Ollama</li>
          <li>German advisory UI</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Engineering Decisions</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Local-first design without cloud dependency in the Alpha</li>
          <li>Framework-independent TypeScript core/domain libraries</li>
          <li>Repository abstraction around SQLite storage</li>
          <li>Narrow, validated Electron preload boundary</li>
          <li>AI integration behind an AIProvider abstraction</li>
          <li>Declarative knowledge packages that cannot execute code</li>
          <li>No automatic internet research during Alpha</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Current Alpha Scope</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Project is still under active development</li>
          <li>Read-only integration for printers, firmware, slicer profiles and imported files</li>
          <li>Automatic internet research and web scraping are disabled</li>
          <li>Features and UX are still evolving</li>
          <li>User-facing AI is German by default</li>
          <li>Code, schemas, tests and developer documentation use English</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Safety Boundaries</h2>
        <p>
          PrintTune is designed as an explanation and recommendation layer. It
          must not send G-code, modify printer settings, restart services, change
          slicer profiles or edit imported source files. When evidence is not
          sufficient, the assistant should say that reliable recommendations
          cannot be made.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>What I Am Learning</h2>
        <p>
          This project helps me practice maintainable desktop application
          architecture, local-first data management, safe local AI integration,
          framework-independent domain logic, validation across application
          boundaries, searchable local knowledge systems and testing
          Electron/React applications.
        </p>
      </section>
    </section>
  </article>
</main>

<%- include("partials/footer") %>
